'' AN ARGUMENT THAT CANNOT CONVERT, AT A CALL WITH ONE CANDIDATE, IS AN ERROR. It came out
'' untyped with nothing said, and lowering dropped the statement: 'print ptrp( y )' over
'' 'byval p as T ptr' with a T value compiled, printed nothing, and reported only
'' '1 statements not lowered'. See src/symbols/argmismatch.bas for why the rule is a list
'' of measured pairs rather than "no candidate".
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source: exactly these lines, and
'' no others --
''
''     34-40  error 58    a UDT value to a pointer, a string, 'byref as zstring', a
''                        procedure pointer
''     41-42  error 24    a pointer to a number
''     43-45  error 58    a pointer to 'byref as long', 'byref as T', 'byref as zstring'
''     46-48  error 24    '@fnp', '@t1' and 'cptr( any ptr, 5 )' to a number
''     49-51  error 24    a long, double and boolean VARIABLE to a pointer
''     52-53  error 58    a string variable and a literal to a UDT with no constructor
''     57     error 58    'this' -- the object -- to a 'T ptr'
''     61     error 24    a NULL pointer constant to a DOUBLE -- it binds an integer only
'' TEST: cli
